# Round 18, C1-38 (fixed): "the key bind of a def, input, place or fill, which is defined for every key" needs no on or over (L §5.6, §5.7 LOAD-ALIVE). The take in pos order gives s1 min(10, 6) = 6 and s2 the rest 4 (L §5.12).
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons
index slots = [s1, s2]
input cap[p in persons]: money PLN
input need[k in slots]: money PLN
fill f[p in persons]
  supply cap[p]
  demand need[k] for k in slots
  arc true
  order pos(k)
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  persons + [ola] lives 1950-01-01..
  cap[ola] = 10
  need[s1] = 6
  need[s2] = 6
ask q: f[ola].taken[k] for k in slots
=== expect
q (k = s1): 6.00 PLN
  cut 2026-12-31
q (k = s2): 4.00 PLN
  cut 2026-12-31
